{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_EOF' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\",\n      \"line\": 4085,\n      \"summary\": \"A whitespace-only rationale passes the within-limit preflight because the shared gate compares the field with the empty string. A structured signed attestation can therefore record a within-limit finding with no reason; require a trimmed non-empty rationale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\n      \"line\": 1192,\n      \"summary\": \"The ready check treats ADR directory read errors as no ADRs and skips unreadable ADR files. A present but unreadable ADR can therefore evade the required limit-reference check; fail closed on I/O errors while preserving the absent-directory case.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R4-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:35-49; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud' passed\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept R1-R4 across accepted-limit parsing and spec qualification; plan and bundle digest omission; brief rendering/versioning; draft-to-attestation mapping and shared preflight; ADR ready-check; English, Portuguese, and scaffold documentation. Ran focused tests and the active planned POSE tools. The design assessment reported no structural deltas.\\\"\n}\n\"'```\n\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\",\"line\":4085,\"summary\":\"A whitespace-only rationale passes the within-limit preflight because the shared gate compares the field with the empty string. A structured signed attestation can therefore record a within-limit finding with no reason; require a trimmed non-empty rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\"line\":1192,\"summary\":\"The ready check treats ADR directory read errors as no ADRs and skips unreadable ADR files. A present but unreadable ADR can therefore evade the required limit-reference check; fail closed on I/O errors while preserving the absent-directory case.\"}],\"prior_findings\":[{\"id\":\"R4-N1\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:35-49; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud' passed\\\"}],\\\"sweep\\\":\\\"Swept R1-R4 across accepted-limit parsing and spec qualification; plan and bundle digest omission; brief rendering/versioning; draft-to-attestation mapping and shared preflight; ADR ready-check; English, Portuguese, and scaffold documentation. Ran focused tests and the active planned POSE tools. The design assessment reported no structural deltas.\\\",\\\"criteria\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Examined the spec's L1 and L2 text. L1 discloses that implementer-written limits can be broad and requires the reviewer to challenge an unjustified limit; L2 binds edits to a new plan and bundle digest. Both assumptions are visible to this independent review, and L1 is an accepted human-review risk.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The accepted_limits and finding.limit fields are optional and omitted when empty, so existing records without limits keep their form. The new brief is versioned as review-brief/11; prior templates remain covered by the immutable-template integration evidence.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The change stays within pose-mcp and extends the shared attestation model. The integration assessment's three HTTP consumer gaps are unrelated to these changed contracts.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-observability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"compatibility\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The digest fields use omitempty when no limits are present, and the tests preserve earlier brief versions. The change is additive for scopes without accepted limits.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"correctness\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"design-causality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The cause in the spec is repeated review rounds without a place to state the assumed environment. R1/R2 parse and seal those assumptions; D1 leaves semantic fit to the reviewer and records the sealed limit plus a reason; D2 makes edits stale the digest. The design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"documentation\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Compared the English and Portuguese manuals with both embedded scaffold copies. Their accepted-limit behavior and review-brief/11 references match runtime; the brief renderer test also covers the new section.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"operability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"requirements\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"R4 fails open on unreadable ADR inputs (N2); R3 also lacks a whitespace-trimmed reason check on the shared within-limit preflight (N1).\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The changed behavior is confined to the accepted-limit parser, review plan and bundle, reviewer brief, attestation gate, ready-check, and matching docs/scaffold artifacts named by the spec.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Compared with prose-only limits, parsing and digest-sealing are the smallest sufficient way to keep later spec edits from changing the reviewed assumptions. Semantic inclusion remains reviewer judgment because automatic natural-language matching would be speculative; no round cap or model-based matcher is added. This choice would need revision if policy requires machine proof that each finding is contained in a limit. The shared preflight must still reject an empty reason.\\\"}],\\\"tools\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exited 0. It reported repository-wide provenance warnings; none identifies a defect in the sealed subject.\"},{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\",\"rationale\":\"Ran the design assessment; it returned zero deltas.\"},{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Ran without persistence; pose-mcp was discovered.\"},{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Ran the integration assessment. Its three unobserved HTTP consumers are outside this change'\"'s boundaries.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The scan was incomplete because two specs were invalid and reported one uncovered repository-wide marker; no new marker was found in the changed implementation.\"},{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI closeout-check spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model\",\"rationale\":\"The check requires a completed attestation, which the review brief explicitly forbids recording.\"},{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI review-check spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model\",\"rationale\":\"The check requires a completed attestation, which the review brief explicitly forbids recording.\"},{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules.\"},{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\",\"rationale\":\"The required surface check exited 0 with one target and no findings.\"},{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The sealed bundle has passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. The attempted strict rerun failed before checks because the read-only sandbox blocked Go temp-directory and cache writes.\"},{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The sealed pose-mcp unit evidence passed, and the focused accepted-limit tests passed. The module validation rerun failed before checks because the read-only sandbox blocked Go temp-directory and cache writes.\"}]}\nPOSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_EOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_EOF' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\",\n      \"line\": 4085,\n      \"summary\": \"A whitespace-only rationale passes the within-limit preflight because the shared gate compares the field with the empty string. A structured signed attestation can therefore record a within-limit finding with no reason; require a trimmed non-empty rationale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\n      \"line\": 1192,\n      \"summary\": \"The ready check treats ADR directory read errors as no ADRs and skips unreadable ADR files. A present but unreadable ADR can therefore evade the required limit-reference check; fail closed on I/O errors while preserving the absent-directory case.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R4-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:35-49; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud' passed\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept R1-R4 across accepted-limit parsing and spec qualification; plan and bundle digest omission; brief rendering/versioning; draft-to-attestation mapping and shared preflight; ADR ready-check; English, Portuguese, and scaffold documentation. Ran focused tests and the active planned POSE tools. The design assessment reported no structural deltas.\\\"\n}\n\"'```\n\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\",\"line\":4085,\"summary\":\"A whitespace-only rationale passes the within-limit preflight because the shared gate compares the field with the empty string. A structured signed attestation can therefore record a within-limit finding with no reason; require a trimmed non-empty rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\"line\":1192,\"summary\":\"The ready check treats ADR directory read errors as no ADRs and skips unreadable ADR files. A present but unreadable ADR can therefore evade the required limit-reference check; fail closed on I/O errors while preserving the absent-directory case.\"}],\"prior_findings\":[{\"id\":\"R4-N1\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:35-49; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud' passed\\\"}],\\\"sweep\\\":\\\"Swept R1-R4 across accepted-limit parsing and spec qualification; plan and bundle digest omission; brief rendering/versioning; draft-to-attestation mapping and shared preflight; ADR ready-check; English, Portuguese, and scaffold documentation. Ran focused tests and the active planned POSE tools. The design assessment reported no structural deltas.\\\",\\\"criteria\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Examined the spec's L1 and L2 text. L1 discloses that implementer-written limits can be broad and requires the reviewer to challenge an unjustified limit; L2 binds edits to a new plan and bundle digest. Both assumptions are visible to this independent review, and L1 is an accepted human-review risk.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The accepted_limits and finding.limit fields are optional and omitted when empty, so existing records without limits keep their form. The new brief is versioned as review-brief/11; prior templates remain covered by the immutable-template integration evidence.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The change stays within pose-mcp and extends the shared attestation model. The integration assessment's three HTTP consumer gaps are unrelated to these changed contracts.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-observability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"compatibility\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The digest fields use omitempty when no limits are present, and the tests preserve earlier brief versions. The change is additive for scopes without accepted limits.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"correctness\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"design-causality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The cause in the spec is repeated review rounds without a place to state the assumed environment. R1/R2 parse and seal those assumptions; D1 leaves semantic fit to the reviewer and records the sealed limit plus a reason; D2 makes edits stale the digest. The design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"documentation\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Compared the English and Portuguese manuals with both embedded scaffold copies. Their accepted-limit behavior and review-brief/11 references match runtime; the brief renderer test also covers the new section.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"operability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"requirements\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"R4 fails open on unreadable ADR inputs (N2); R3 also lacks a whitespace-trimmed reason check on the shared within-limit preflight (N1).\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The changed behavior is confined to the accepted-limit parser, review plan and bundle, reviewer brief, attestation gate, ready-check, and matching docs/scaffold artifacts named by the spec.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Compared with prose-only limits, parsing and digest-sealing are the smallest sufficient way to keep later spec edits from changing the reviewed assumptions. Semantic inclusion remains reviewer judgment because automatic natural-language matching would be speculative; no round cap or model-based matcher is added. This choice would need revision if policy requires machine proof that each finding is contained in a limit. The shared preflight must still reject an empty reason.\\\"}],\\\"tools\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check -