{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"agent_message","text":"**Decision: changes requested.** I found two medium blockers.\n\n- [review_bundle.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1205443169/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:4085): the within-limit preflight accepts whitespace-only rationale on the structured attestation path.\n- [lintspec.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1205443169/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1192): ADR read errors are treated as no ADRs, so the ready check can pass without verifying required limit references.\n\nThe prior finding R4-N1 is fixed: the parser now requires an assumption and a reason in the same sentence. The focused tests passed. Strict validation could not reach Go checks because the read-only sandbox blocked Go temporary-directory and cache access; the sealed bundle contains passing validation evidence. The worktree is clean, and no attestation was recorded.\n\n| Criterion | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300` |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\n| backend-contracts | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration` |\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration` |\n| backend-observability | failed (N2) | N2 |\n| compatibility | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration` |\n| correctness | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300` |\n| documentation | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration` |\n| operability | failed (N2) | N2 |\n| requirements | failed (N2) | N2 |\n| scope | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\n| security | failed (N1) | N1 |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300` |\n\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\",\n      \"line\": 4085,\n      \"summary\": \"A whitespace-only rationale passes the within-limit preflight because the shared gate compares the field with the empty string. A structured signed attestation can therefore record a within-limit finding with no reason; require a trimmed non-empty rationale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\n      \"line\": 1192,\n      \"summary\": \"The ready check treats ADR directory read errors as no ADRs and skips unreadable ADR files. A present but unreadable ADR can therefore evade the required limit-reference check; fail closed on I/O errors while preserving the absent-directory case.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R4-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:35-49; go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud' passed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept R1-R4 across accepted-limit parsing and spec qualification; plan and bundle digest omission; brief rendering/versioning; draft-to-attestation mapping and shared preflight; ADR ready-check; English, Portuguese, and scaffold documentation. Ran focused tests and the active planned POSE tools. The design assessment reported no structural deltas.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the spec's L1 and L2 text. L1 discloses that implementer-written limits can be broad and requires the reviewer to challenge an unjustified limit; L2 binds edits to a new plan and bundle digest. Both assumptions are visible to this independent review, and L1 is an accepted human-review risk.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The accepted_limits and finding.limit fields are optional and omitted when empty, so existing records without limits keep their form. The new brief is versioned as review-brief/11; prior templates remain covered by the immutable-template integration evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change stays within pose-mcp and extends the shared attestation model. The integration assessment's three HTTP consumer gaps are unrelated to these changed contracts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The digest fields use omitempty when no limits are present, and the tests preserve earlier brief versions. The change is additive for scopes without accepted limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The cause in the spec is repeated review rounds without a place to state the assumed environment. R1/R2 parse and seal those assumptions; D1 leaves semantic fit to the reviewer and records the sealed limit plus a reason; D2 makes edits stale the digest. The design assessment observed no structural delta.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the English and Portuguese manuals with both embedded scaffold copies. Their accepted-limit behavior and review-brief/11 references match runtime; the brief renderer test also covers the new section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R4 fails open on unreadable ADR inputs (N2); R3 also lacks a whitespace-trimmed reason check on the shared within-limit preflight (N1).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The changed behavior is confined to the accepted-limit parser, review plan and bundle, reviewer brief, attestation gate, ready-check, and matching docs/scaffold artifacts named by the spec.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared with prose-only limits, parsing and digest-sealing are the smallest sufficient way to keep later spec edits from changing the reviewed assumptions. Semantic inclusion remains reviewer judgment because automatic natural-language matching would be speculative; no round cap or model-based matcher is added. This choice would need revision if policy requires machine proof that each finding is contained in a limit. The shared preflight must still reject an empty reason.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exited 0. It reported repository-wide provenance warnings; none identifies a defect in the sealed subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-2aa7dc50d363d300\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the design assessment; it returned zero deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence; pose-mcp was discovered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the integration assessment. Its three unobserved HTTP consumers are outside this change's boundaries.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two specs were invalid and reported one uncovered repository-wide marker; no new marker was found in the changed implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI closeout-check spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The check requires a completed attestation, which the review brief explicitly forbids recording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI review-check spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The check requires a completed attestation, which the review brief explicitly forbids recording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required surface check exited 0 with one target and no findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The sealed bundle has passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. The attempted strict rerun failed before checks because the read-only sandbox blocked Go temp-directory and cache writes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The sealed pose-mcp unit evidence passed, and the focused accepted-limit tests passed. The module validation rerun failed before checks because the read-only sandbox blocked Go temp-directory and cache writes.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
